title: "A rational counterexample to the reciprocal-logarithmic assertion in Erdős problem 143"
authors:
  - family-names: Apicella
    given-names: Mattia
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mapice/erdos-143-candidate-disproof"
url: "https://github.com/mapice/erdos-143-candidate-disproof"
abstract: >-
  Paper and Lean 4 formalization of a rational set separated by at least one
  from all positive integer dilates of its distinct elements, with divergent
  reciprocal-logarithmic sum. Local kernel checks and a 245-declaration axiom
  audit passed; independent expert review remains pending.
keywords:
  - Erdos problem 143
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - primitive sets
  - analytic number theory
